# --- Environments ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# .env.ci: placeholders generated by ci.yml's `infra` job so it can run
# `docker compose config` (the compose uses ${VAR:?} and fails without the vars). It is
# ephemeral on the runner, but reproducing the step locally leaves an un-ignored .env.* in
# git status — and a trackable .env.* is how a secret gets committed by accident.
.env.ci
!.env.example
# `infra/host/secrets.env.sops` is NOT in this repository and is not supposed to be.
# ADR 0036 §4 turned the accident into the decision: the encrypted file is generated ON THE
# HOST by infra/host/scripts/secrets-bootstrap.sh and stays there, untracked. With a single
# age recipient, a versioned ciphertext helps in exactly one scenario — the host is gone —
# and in that scenario the private key needed to read it is gone with it.
#
# The negation below is kept ON PURPOSE even though nothing matches it. It costs nothing and
# it documents that if the file ever DOES get committed (a second offline recipient would
# make that worth doing), no future `.env*` rule silently swallows it. Do not read it as a
# claim that the file is versioned today — it is not.
!infra/host/secrets.env.sops

